WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.120
President Trump is finally putting a
team in place that could begin to

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.780
address the grave and growing security
threats right here in our hemisphere: the

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.670
corrupt narco-state in Venezuela; the
explosion of coca in Colombia; and the

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:22.720
attack on democratic institutions in
Central America by narco kingpins and

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.130
gangs. They're even backing the election
of an anti-American candidate in Mexico –

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.570
Imagine another failed state like
Venezuela right on our doorstep. As

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:36.249
Secretary of State, Mike Pompeo can form a diplomatic team of experienced and

00:00:36.249 --> 00:00:40.870
loyal political appointees who can lead
and manage career diplomats to confront

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.440
threats, rather than kick the can down
the road. They should press for an urgent

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.940
transition in Venezuela, rallying the
region to sanction the Maduro regime and

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.199
support democratic opposition, and they
must help Colombia's next president

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:57.399
confront the persistent narco terrorist
threat. And they should reassure Mexico

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:00.219
that the United States will be a
reliable partner, growing together

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:04.119
economically and tending to common
security threats. The new foreign policy

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
team must begin to take care of business
right here in our neighborhood.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.560
What do you think about President Trump's new foreign policy team and US leadership

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.680
here in the Americas? Let us know in your
comments. And also let us know if there

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.520
are other topics that you'd like
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:28.080
sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

